WEBVTT

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.890
<i>Back when I was a young student,</i>
<i>I watched a foreign movie.</i>

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.810
<i>I still remember the party scene</i>
<i>on a luxury cruise ship.</i>

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:28.110
<i>I was deeply impressed by</i>
<i>how gorgeous and exquisite it was.</i>

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.400
<i>"I want to join such a party someday.</i>

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.410
<i>To make it happen,</i>
<i>I will work my way up in society!"</i>

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.950
<i>It might have been my youth</i>
<i>that motivated me that way.</i>

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.870
<i>Decades have passed since then.</i>

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.120
KAZUO YAMASHITA
PRESIDENT, YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.790
<i>I wish I could tell my young self...</i>
<i>that one day my dream would come true!</i>

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.380
<i>Although it comes with a huge debt.</i>

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.230
This is a whole different world to me.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.480
OHMA TOKITA
FIGHTER, YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.400
-I prefer the other ship to this one.
-Mr. Yamashita, Ohma.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.860
Mr. Nogi!

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.530
HIDEKI NOGI
CHAIRMAN, NOGI GROUP

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.540
It's been a while, Ohma. Congratulations
on getting through to the tournament.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.960
I won my place in the tournament myself,
the way you suggested.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.880
But that doesn't mean
that I'm going to be your pawn.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:06.970
PULLING STRINGS

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.020
Come on, Kaede. Don't be so heartless.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.480
KAEDE AKIYAMA,
CHAIRMAN'S SECRETARY, NOGI GROUP

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.980
-Can I get your number at least?
-You're being too persistent, Lihito.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:22.160
Besides, shouldn't you
be with your employer right now?

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.910
My employer?

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.660
I don't have one. I'm on my own.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.870
As a matter of fact,
I'm the president of SH Frozen Storage.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.920
LIHITO
PRESIDENT AND FIGHTER, SH FROZEN STORAGE

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.880
What?

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:37.670
Does that mean
you're a president and a fighter?

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.550
Surprised?

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.010
I wouldn't be here
if it wasn't for your boss,

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.680
-Chairman Nogi.
-Hey. Get away from me.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.520
<i>I was fired as a fighter</i>

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.100
<i>and got a part-time job</i>
<i>for a shipping company under Nogi Group.</i>

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.770
<i>They paid me well.</i>

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.730
<i>Then one day,</i>
<i>Nogi visited me unexpectedly.</i>

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.950
<i>His words made me snap out of my stupor.</i>

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:07.870
<i>Lihito, you're not the type of person</i>
<i>who deserves to work under others.</i>

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.250
<i>You should start your own company at once.</i>

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.080
<i>You think so too?</i>

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.920
<i>I'll entrust you with a food company</i>
<i>we bought out recently.</i>

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.050
<i>Wow! But hold on a second.</i>

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.090
<i>Being a president does appeal to me,</i>
<i>but I want to be a fighter again.</i>

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.260
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.600
<i>You'll make a comeback</i>
<i>as the first ever "president fighter."</i>

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.810
<i>Wow. The first ever?</i>
<i>That sounds awesome!</i>

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.060
<i>-You just need to sign this contract.</i>
<i>-Okay!</i>

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.520
<i>-I'll lend you as much money as you need.</i>
<i>-Okay!</i>

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.690
<i>All you'll need is the challenge fee</i>
<i>to get membership</i>

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.900
<i>and then the entry fee to the tournament.</i>

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.570
<i>-It's not very much at all.</i>
<i>-Okay!</i>

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.660
<i>-It's only five billion yen in total.</i>
<i>-Okay!</i>

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.880
That's how I made
a sudden comeback to kengan matches.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.000
<i>He's been conned.</i>

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.010
You've succeeded then.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.380
-So, if you win...
-He won't.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.010
...will you become the chairman
of the Kengan Association?

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.390
What? Don't you know anything?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.350
If I win the tournament,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:17.100
-I must designate Nogi as the chairman.
-What?

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:21.110
-It's part of the contract.
-Designate him?

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.070
-Is that allowed, Ms. Akiyama?
-Yes.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.780
The reward for winning the tournament
is the right to designate the chairman.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.960
The choice of the next chairman
is in the hands of the winning company.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.870
Yamashita Corporation
has the same contract.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:41.670
The more participants you control,
the more of an advantage you have.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:46.010
Mr. Nogi didn't tell me any of this.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.470
<i>Wait a second.</i>

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.850
Ms. Akiyama, does that mean...

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:57.060
I suppose other companies
are probably using the same tactics as us.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:01.440
<i>Many companies drag other companies</i>
<i>into their own camp</i>

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.150
<i>through buyouts,</i>
<i>conciliation and coercion.</i>

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.660
<i>This is what will be</i>
<i>happening behind the scenes.</i>

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.740
This tournament is essentially
a stratagem battle between companies

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.830
to secure the position of chairman.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.710
-Basically, we just need to win.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.180
I don't feel comfortable
in a fancy place like this.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.760
What's going on there?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.440
NAOYA OHKUBO
FIGHTER, MUJI TELEVISION NETWORK

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:43.150
<i>That's the absolute champion</i>
<i>of ultimate fighting, Naoya Ohkubo.</i>

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.360
<i>Wait, why are they playing Japanese chess?</i>

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.900
Hey, Kazu!

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:48.740
Ken!

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.240
KEN OHYA
GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP CHAIRMAN

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.780
-I've been looking for you.
-Is everything all right?

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.330
Kazu, you're good
at Japanese chess, aren't you?

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.120
Well, yeah. I believe so.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.250
Avenge me and beat him.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.500
I can't win
no matter how many times I try.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.760
Really? You lost against Ohkubo?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.760
Not him. That guy!

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.140
There. That's checkmate.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:17.270
Goddamn it! Why can't I win?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.020
SUEKICHI KANEDA
JAPANESE CHESS PLAYER

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.560
Well, too bad.
I look forward to your next challenge.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:26.320
Now, is there anyone else
who would like to challenge me?

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.070
The challenge fee is 10,000 yen.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.150
If you win, I will give you 100,000 yen...

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.070
Gambling on Japanese chess? Here?
Who is he anyway?

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.200
That's my friend, Suekichi Kaneda.
He's from outside of the kengan world.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.040
Why did you bring an outsider here?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:46.040
I met him at a Japanese chess center
yesterday and we became friends.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:48.670
<i>We went for drinks and really hit it off.</i>

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.050
<i>I invited him on the spur of the moment.</i>

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:56.930
Oh? Mr. Ohya.
Is that the man you were talking about?

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.770
Yes, this is Mr. Yamashita.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.690
He has 50 years’ experience
in Japanese chess.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:07.270
Wow. You must really be a tough one.
I hope you go easy on me.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:10.990
<i>This guy must underestimate me.</i>

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:12.820
All right.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.370
Let me show you my skills.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:20.500
People used to call me
"Kazu the Twisting Rook." Behold.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.120
There. Checkmate.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.130
What!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.460
That's the fifth time
in a row that I've lost!

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:31.090
Don't beat yourself up so much.
You did a fine job.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:34.970
Even Kazu couldn't match him.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.050
<i>He's pretty good.</i>

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:38.970
TAKAYUKI CHIBA
FIGHTER, YOSHITAKE REAL ESTATE

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.390
<i>It's as if he can see</i>
<i>his opponent's every move in advance.</i>

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:44.600
Hey, look. Isn't that Chairman Katahara?

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.270
-It's him!
-It's Chairman Katahara!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.940
What's he doing up there?

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.200
Thank you all for waiting.
Let's get started.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:57.200
METSUDO KATAHARA, GOVERNOR OF DAINIPPON
BANK & KENGAN ASSOCIATION CHAIRMAN

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.700
SEN HATSUMI
FIGHTER, NOGI GROUP

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.540
Here he is, the monster geezer.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.330
The ship will arrive at the battlefield

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.460
in about 27 hours from now.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.880
Twenty-seven hours? That's a long trip.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:16.550
Upon arriving at the battlefield,
you must register your fighters.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.520
This will see them entered officially
into the Kengan Life-or-Death Tournament.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.520
Entered officially? What does that mean?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.480
One more thing.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:32.780
Private battles between kengan fighters
on this ship are firmly prohibited.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.700
Those who break this order will
be sanctioned by the Guards.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.780
THE GUARDS
PRIVATE ARMY OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.570
That's all.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:44.040
You may return to enjoying the voyage.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:47.170
<i>I see. This is just...</i>

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.670
Perfect.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:53.050
-Nogi.
-Oh! It's been a long time.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.960
SHION SORYUIN
CHAIRWOMAN, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.470
-Ms. Soryuin.
-Let's skip the pleasantries.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.930
What did you think
of the chairman's speech?

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:04.100
Oh. You noticed, too?

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.810
Do you think something triggered it?

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:10.270
Who knows? The Kengan Association
is full of ambitious people.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:11.820
Ambitious people?

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.780
-Are you talking about yourself?
-You're as sexy as ever.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:17.780
-Huh. Ohma Tokita.
-Wow! He's hot!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.490
Huh? Do I know you?

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.830
You're even more handsome close up.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.160
I can see why our fighter,
Kiryu, is chasing after you.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.840
Setsuna Kiryu. Where is that asshole?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.590
Oh no! Ms. Soryuin!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.970
Don't lose your cool, boy.
Are you trying to hit on me?

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.470
What are you doing, Tokita?

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:47.640
I don't know what kind of history
you guys have, but I can tell you this.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.980
He is extraordinarily strong.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:56.650
<i>If you want to fight him, you should</i>
<i>prepare yourself to some extent.</i>

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.650
SETSUNA KIRYU
FIGHTER, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:01.160
What the hell are you?

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:06.660
Blood splatter from the blow you struck
fell on him and defiled his body.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.330
You should die.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.090
Yes, companies are allowed to change

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.590
the fighter they have
chosen to represent them.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:20.550
What?

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.010
RYO HIMURO
GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.930
Are you kidding me right now, Kaneda?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.720
Oh, no. That's not my intention at all.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.980
So, I'll ask you one more time,
Mr. Himuro.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:36.270
Will you allow me
to represent you instead?

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.580
You want to be our fighter?

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.790
What's wrong with you, Kaneda?

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.330
-It's too late to switch--
-No, it's not.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:58.090
The chairman mentioned two things
in his speech which caught my attention.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:03.340
The first thing was that the fighters are
only officially registered upon arrival.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:07.010
To put it another way,

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:11.980
until we arrive at our destination,
you are allowed to change your fighters.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:13.560
That can't be true.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:17.520
Don't you remember he also said private
battles weren't allowed on the ship?

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:24.530
What he actually said was that battles
between kengan fighters are forbidden.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:26.780
That brings me to the second thing.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.950
Battles with outsiders are not prohibited.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.870
If you want proof of that,
look over there.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.500
Those Guards are watching
me organize a private battle

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.550
yet they're making
no attempt to try to stop me.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.380
Oh my God.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.300
I didn't think there could be a loophole
like this in the passenger-on-board rule.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.560
Hey, Himuro!

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:53.600
Don't worry, Mr. Ohya.
I won't harm your friend.

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:56.400
I'll get this done in no time.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.150
You're scaring me!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.690
<i>He's not bluffing, he's perfectly serious.</i>

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:06.110
All right, then. Let's get started.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.580
The winner will represent Ginokuniya
Bookshop. Is that okay with you?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:14.040
It's not like I have
anything against you or--

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.840
Don't be vain.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.750
You are no match for me.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.970
<i>He's fast and he's a southpaw.</i>

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.470
I'll give you one minute.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.680
If you can withstand my attacks
for one minute,

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.680
you can be their fighter.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:35.940
That's very kind of you.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.940
I'm not going to pull any punches.
You should prepare yourself.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.240
<i>It's okay. This isn't a problem.</i>

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:48.490
<i>I just need to watch out for his left fist</i>
<i>while I analyze his--</i>

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:52.200
<i>That was a vertical fist!</i>

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.590
<i>No, I was wrong. He's not a southpaw.</i>

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.340
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.170
Mr. Himuro,

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:08.760
you practice Jeet Kune Do, don't you?

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.850
<i>Jeet Kune Do is a modern martial art</i>
<i>based on Chinese Kung Fu</i>

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:17.100
<i>which has ambiguous fighting tactics.</i>

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:20.190
<i>It uses a stance</i>
<i>with the dominant arm and leg forward</i>

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.190
<i>and unique trapping techniques.</i>

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:25.030
<i>It allows all kinds of forbidden moves,</i>
<i>such as poking eyes,</i>

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.150
<i>attacking the groin and kicking joints.</i>

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.660
<i>The battles are kept brief and short.</i>

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:33.530
<i>The average match lasts</i>
<i>for a mere six seconds.</i>

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:35.830
<i>It's my balance.</i>

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:40.000
<i>He worked that out by observing</i>
<i>the position of my center of gravity.</i>

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.920
You have a keen eye.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.340
Good luck with that.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.010
Feel free to surrender
as soon as you've had enough.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:00.730
<i>Is he just going to defend himself</i>
<i>for the whole minute?</i>

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.860
Don't underestimate me.
Die, sucker!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:11.280
<i>Whoa, Himuro. Don't take it too far.</i>

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.830
<i>He got him right in the ribs!</i>

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:26.920
I hope you get it now, Kaneda.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.880
Kengan matches are no game.
So don't joke around.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:36.390
<i>Is he serious?</i>
<i>Does he still think he can win?</i>

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.690
<i>Kaneda hit Himuro.</i>

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.820
It looks like I scored a bull's eye.

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:52.160
<i>What the hell?</i>
<i>How did he manage to hit me?</i>

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:55.990
How was that? I'm not that bad, am I?

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.240
You freaking newbie.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.710
You're getting too cocky.
Playtime's over.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.340
I'm going to ask you again.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:16.760
Will you allow me to represent
Ginokuniya Bookshop instead?

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:21.100
<i>What's happening?</i>
<i>How did he beat me?</i>

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.440
I'm so tired.
Why don't we have a little break?

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.360
<i>Himuro.</i>

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.740
<i>He's got serious.</i>

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:35.990
I admit it.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.950
You're strong.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.410
<i>What a murderous expression on his face.</i>

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:48.840
<i>What is the most powerful weapon</i>
<i>in Jeet Kune Do?</i>

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:51.920
<i>Is it breaking a joint?</i>
<i>Or kicking the groin?</i>

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.470
<i>No. The answer is...</i>

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:58.760
<i>the combination</i>
<i>of the fastest and the shortest.</i>

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:02.770
<i>The average punch velocity</i>
<i>of a middleweight boxer</i>

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.350
<i>is ten meters per second.</i>

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:10.190
<i>Himuro's punch velocity however,</i>
<i>is an outstanding 15 meters per second.</i>

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.900
<i>Furthermore, he can shift</i>
<i>to the offensive in an instant</i>

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.070
<i>while still blocking</i>
<i>his opponent's attacks.</i>

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:22.290
<i>It makes the opponent experience</i>
<i>his punches faster than they actually are.</i>

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.880
<i>Eye jab? He's trying to kill me!</i>

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.380
That's enough, Himuro!
Kaneda can't take anymore.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.880
It's over now.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:41.760
<i>Perfect! That felt amazing.</i>
<i>But he did make it difficult...</i>

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.230
<i>What?</i>

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:48.480
<i>Thank you, Mr. Himuro.</i>

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.980
<i>Now I'm the winner.</i>

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:57.530
He broke his arm!

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.910
My timing was perfect. How?

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.370
Wow. That must hurt a lot.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:13.420
So, what do you say?
Do you want to continue?

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.680
Kaneda, I'm going to kill you!

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:19.550
You can stop now, Himuro!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.260
Even you can't fight with only one arm.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:28.060
<i>He hit his broken arm!</i>

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:32.900
<i>Suddenly, Himuro's blows</i>
<i>stopped landing on Kaneda.</i>

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.940
<i>What kind of trick is Kaneda using?</i>

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:39.860
<i>What the hell was that?</i>

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.780
<i>Kaneda dodged Himuro's kick</i>
<i>faster than he could deliver it?</i>

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.790
<i>No way!</i>

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:51.790
<i>Blow to the liver in one second.</i>
<i>One and a half steps back.</i>

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.000
<i>And... he missed it.</i>

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:59.010
<i>I can't believe that Kaneda can actually</i>
<i>predict Himuro's every move.</i>

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.390
<i>Is that even possible?</i>

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.430
Can we finish this now?

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:09.140
It took me a while,
but I can read your every move now.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:12.100
You've already been checkmated.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.770
It's not cool to go on struggling in vain.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.650
Why don't you just concede?

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.200
Shut up!

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.990
<i>Of course, it had to end like this.</i>

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:27.870
<i>The Kujin Style...</i>

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:31.620
Falling Bucket.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.430
Kaneda.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.850
You should have had
enough by now, Mr. Himuro.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:51.020
Just stay lying there.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:54.270
Stop, Kaneda! That's enough!

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:00.150
<i>Mr. Himuro. You're incredible.</i>

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.620
<i>I admire your tenacity</i>
<i>and determination to triumph.</i>

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.950
<i>However, this is checkmate.</i>

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:15.960
<i>Himuro was the strongest fighter</i>
<i>our company has ever had.</i>

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:21.840
<i>But he still lost... to this unknown man.</i>

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:24.550
<i>So what?</i>

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:28.430
<i>Being strong is absolute</i>
<i>and the only truth.</i>

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:32.600
Kaneda, why don't you become our fighter?

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.730
RYO HIMURO
FIGHTER, GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.980
SUEKICHI KANEDA
FIGHTER, GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:45.410
Hey, Tokita. I've been looking for you.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.700
I'm digesting my food.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:50.240
People are holding
so many parties on this ship.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:53.580
Free food and drink is awesome.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:55.210
By the way, did you hear?

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:00.000
Ginokuniya's fighter, Himuro,
was defeated by a stranger.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:02.920
Who is this Kaneda guy?

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:07.300
Actually, should we
be worried about ourselves?

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:12.430
It turns out battles are allowed as long
as they're not between kengan fighters.

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:13.600
Who cares?

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.980
What? You should, Tokita.

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:21.440
It means we run the risk
of being attacked by somebody.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:26.990
Thank you for coming.

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.870
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI
FIGHTER, FURUMI PHARMA

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:29.830
You'd better mean it.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:31.790
COSMO IMAI
FIGHTER, NISHIHONJI SECURITY SERVICES

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:35.500
-I was in the middle of having dinner.
-Could you stop eating for a moment?

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.920
Strange. What is it?

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:45.220
The rules of this tournament allow
for collusion, bribery and intimidation.

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:49.850
I don't see how those
rules benefit the chairman.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:53.350
So, you're wondering why
he has those rules?

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:58.150
Who's behind all this?
And who can we trust?

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:00.770
Misjudging this could cost us our lives.

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:05.150
Here they come already.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.870
Look. They're kengan fighters.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:13.370
Let's crush them and take their spots.

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:14.870
MISFORTUNE

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.330
Well, I guess my plan to talk to you
covertly has worked against me.

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:23.300
No. This is perfect.
I was getting bored of this voyage.

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:28.050
Whoa. Don't you have any sense of danger?

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:32.470
Well, looks like it's time
for a little workout.

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:35.020
Let's do this.

00:24:06.070 --> 00:24:06.940
PREVIEW

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.190
<i>This is the battlefield</i>
<i>of the tournament, Ganryu Island.</i>

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:14.780
<i>Men, women, geniuses, gods and demons.</i>

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:16.160
<i>The time has come.</i>

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:19.580
<i>Spin the roulette wheel of fate.</i>
<i>Next episode: "The Night Before"</i>

00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:21.000
Subtitle translation by
Miki Miyaji
